\documentclass{article}
\title{Drift Limits for Soft-Storey Buildings}
\author{V. Anagnostou}
\date{April 2026}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section{Observed Damage}
Post-earthquake reconnaissance repeatedly identifies the same failure pattern.
\item Soft storeys concentrate the drift demand in a single level,
which exhausts the local ductility supply of the columns long before the rest
of the structure is damaged.
Redundant lateral systems redistribute the demand across floors
and prevent the formation of a single storey mechanism.
\end{document}

